    "id": "/",
    "text": "",
    "title": "MYCC",
    "summary": "## MYCC (Mindmap Knowledge System)\n\nThe MYCC section covers `MYCC.md` — the project's self-description doc — and the autonomous knowledge-discovery system that compiles it into a structured, LLM-enriched tree called the **mindmap**, stored at `.mycc/mindmap.json`. Compilation is one-way: `MYCC.md → [compile_mindmap] → mindmap.json`, with process isolation (each agent has its own instance).\n\n**Data model** (`src/mindmap/types.ts`): Nodes with slash-separated `id`, `text`, `title`, LLM `summary`, `level`, `children`, directional `links` (target_type: node/file/url/term). Two in-memory-only flags (`is_mycc`, `is_patch`) drive compile and patch-rebuild logic.\n\n**Compilation / Exploration** (`compile.ts`, `explorer-agent.ts`): `/mindmap compile` parses markdown (code-block-aware) and summarizes nodes via an autonomous **Explorer Agent** using **A-N-C-E** context and **TriologueLite**. It uses 9 tools, a 25-round budget (force-stop at 5), per-message JSONL transcripts, and a tools-free retryChat fallback. Compilation is rotation-based (`.new`/`.bak` atomic save), lock-resumable (4h freshness), and dependency-aware parallel (semaphore, max 3 concurrent).\n\n**Patch system** (`patch-jsonl.ts`, `patch.ts`): agent-discovered knowledge is recorded append-only in `.mycc/mindmap-patch.jsonl` (add/update/delete), validated and replayed via `applyPatchAction`. `/mindmap compile` rebuilds patches (BFS) and preserves MYCC.md-deleted nodes as `add` patches.\n\n**Agent interface** (`recall.ts`): queries the tree, hoists root \"Key Terms\", marks children `[M]`/`[P]`.",
    "level": 0,
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "/mycc.md",
        "text": "This file provides guidance for Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.",
        "title": "MYCC.md",
        "summary": "MYCC.md is the primary guidance document for Claude Code working in the mycc repository — a Node.js coding agent using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference (embedding always via Ollama), with AgentContext as its central state container (ParentContext for main, ChildContext for child/IPC).\n\n**Architecture**: State-machine agent loop (PROMPT/COLLECT/LLM/HOOK/TOOL/STOP states in `src/loop/states/`); Triologue now a thin facade over `src/loop/triologue/` modules (store, pending-tools, compact, wrap-up, checkpoint, tp-fix); AgentIO singleton (I/O, ESC/neglected mode, bang mode); IPC/IOC for main↔child; unified Loader (built-in > project > user); Sequence, Confusion Index (hint rounds), mindmap, wiki (LanceDB), auto-claim, health-check.\n\n**Key terms**: tools/skills/hooks/routine; session/turn/chat; PROMPT vs prompt; autofly/streak; backlog (JSONL) vs livelog + TP constraint; checkpoint/recap; Grant System intent language (dangerous=i_know / batch=i_know escapes); hookish skills with `when` conditions compiled via LLM translation + jsep AST (no eval); Loop Notation (LN); sealed-session principle; steering/file-upload (WebUI); pinned-todo reactivation.\n\n**WebUI** (`src/serve/serve-hub.ts`, `src/web/`): Vue 3 + WebSocket, cards, teammate accordion, `/history`.\n\n**Development**: vitest, tmux/psmux testing, ESLint `no-console-in-tools`, debug flags, Docker, Windows/PowerShell notes, built-in skills table. Pitfalls: DeepSeek limits, child agentIO constraints, tool-description guidance.",
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/project-overview",
            "text": "This project builds a tool called \"mycc\" -- A node.js coding agent implementation using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference. The architecture follows a modular design with AgentContext as the central state container. Two API providers are supported: Ollama (full features including web_search, screen, read_picture) and DeepSeek (cloud-based, no web/screen tools but with prompt caching). Embedding for wiki/RAG always uses Ollama regardless of provider.",
            "title": "Project Overview",
            "summary": "The Project Overview introduces **mycc** (`@pkubangbang/mycc`, v0.10.4 per package.json), a Node.js coding agent using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference. Architecture is modular with **AgentContext** (`src/types.ts`) as the central state container exposing modules: core, todo, mail, skill, issue, bg, team, wiki, and peer. Two implementations exist: ParentContext (lead, direct access) and ChildContext (teammates, IPC wrappers). Two API providers are supported: **Ollama** (full features: webSearch/webFetch, imgDescribe vision, screen/read_picture) and **DeepSeek** (cloud, no web/screen/vision but with prompt caching and thinking mode). Provider selection is in `src/config.ts` via `getApiProvider()` reading the `API_PROVIDER` env var (with model defaults: `glm-5:cloud` Ollama, `deepseek-v4-pro` DeepSeek). `src/engine/chat-provider.ts` statically imports both providers and re-exports the active one at module load, including `forkChat` for prompt-cache-preserving side chats. The RAG embedding facade (`src/engine/rag-provider.ts`) always uses Ollama regardless of chat provider, auto-inferring nomic vs embeddinggemma from `OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_MODEL` (default nomic-embed-text), with NAMESPACE isolating LanceDB tables. Process architecture: Terminal → Coordinator (`src/index.ts`) → Lead → Teammates.",
